 <iati-activity default-currency="EUR" hierarchy="1" iati-activities:version="2.03" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities">
  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000006340</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for WRI Strategic Plan 2022-2028.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This six-year grant proposal concerns core support to the World Resources Institute (WRI), on the basis of its 5-year strategy and a oneyear addendum and other relevant WRI activities. The Netherlands recognizes WRI as an important strategic partner to achieve its policy agenda on sustainable development and climate action in developing countries. WRI is recognized as a critical player in the global environment and development space, and a great communicator with unique convening power. WRI has a growing focus on Africa and a strong network in important emerging markets. Its 5-year strategy closely aligns with the Dutch policy agenda on sustainable development and climate action worldwide. Through support to WRI, the Netherlands aims to make an essential contribution to science-based knowledge and innovative approaches that will benefit people, nature and climate. The six-year grant enables WRI to use its expertise to assist developing countries in building more sustainable and resilient development pathways. Funding also includes (max) USD 5 mln. support till 2025 to the NDC Partnership (NDCP) in order to better integrate adaptation and water into Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs). In addition, funding includes USD 9,8 million for 5 years for Partnering for Green Growth and the Global Goals 2030 (P4G). P4G supports green partnerships to deliver inclusive and sustainable growth. Details regarding NDCP and P4G will be described in additional short memos.</narrative>
  </description>
